{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"87eae90fb7cd26a5ddbf29f2e75d5bf43a69606e319c8baef047d6cee03704b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","key_entities":["infra/scripts/observability.sh","aws cloudwatch put-metric-data","offset file","replication","voter","merge-change","deploy","shared autodeploy-marker","G2P","tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py","tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py"],"problem_keywords":["cumulative counter","offset acknowledgement","metric data loss","cloudwatch publish","transient failure","observability","metrics"],"propositions":["Cumulative error counter offset files are advanced before CloudWatch put-metric-data succeeds, causing transient publish failures to permanently lose the failed interval's metric count.","Seven metric streams across six code shapes (replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, shared deferral/interrupt helper, G2P) share the same defective offset-acknowledgement ordering.","Offset must advance only after successful AWS publication; on failure the offset remains byte-identical to enable retry with accumulated delta on next run.","A whole-script PATH-shim regression test parameterized across all seven streams reproduces the defect (publishes zero instead of accumulated delta after transient failure) before fix and confirms resolution after repair."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787503564859716001,"uuid":"94b8cce9-072a-4eae-82e3-67e0957e816d"}